# Build-context exclusions for `docker build -f Dockerfile .`
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (verify-report CRITICAL-15). There was no
# `.dockerignore`, so `COPY web/ .` in the web-builder stage carried
# `web/test/fixtures/export` — the golden fixture whose own `source.txt` opens
# with "MOST OF THE NUMBERS IN THIS DIRECTORY ARE SYNTHESISED. They were never
# published by INE" — into the image build. The loader's fallback then read it,
# and the shipped image rendered a straight-line invention as INE statistics.
#
# The primary fix is in `web/src/lib/export/loader.ts`: the build now REFUSES
# to guess an artifact source. This file is defence in depth, and it is worth
# having on its own terms: data that never enters the build context cannot be
# published by any future mistake, however the code is rewritten. Both layers
# are required — neither is a substitute for the other.
#
# ADR-5 fixes the context at the repository ROOT (the Go module and the
# `//go:embed config` shim both live there and `//go:embed` cannot traverse
# upwards), so this file, not a narrower context, is the only way to keep the
# test trees out.
#
# Everything the Dockerfile actually reads is listed in its own COPY lines:
# go.mod, go.sum, app/, config/, config_embed.go, and web/. Anything below is
# either not one of those, or a subtree of one that the build does not need.

# ---- Version control and CI ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.atl

# ---- Documentation and specifications --------------------------------------
# Never copied, and the largest source of context bloat in this repository.
docs
openspec
*.md

# ---- Host-side tooling and local state -------------------------------------
scripts
backups
.playwright-mcp
*.png
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# ---- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` holds the real POSTGRES_PASSWORD. A build context is not a secret
# store: anything here is readable in the image's own build layers.
.env
.env.*

# ---- Go test material ------------------------------------------------------
# `go build` ignores `_test.go` files, and the recorded INE/Eurostat payloads
# under testdata/ are only ever read by tests. Excluded so the go-builder stage
# copies production sources only.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata

# ---- Web: everything the production `astro build` does not read -------------
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/.astro
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/blob-report
web/playwright/.cache

# THE POINT OF THIS FILE. `web/test/fixtures/export` lives under here, and so
# does every other fixture. `astro build` reads `src/`, `public/` and the
# config files at the web root; it never reads these, and after this exclusion
# an image build CANNOT reach the synthetic fixture even if a future edit
# reinstates a fallback that points at it.
#
# `web/src/styles/theme.css` declares `@source not "../../test/**"` and
# `@source not "../../tests/**"` for Tailwind's candidate scanner; those
# directives are harmless when the directories are absent (verified by a real
# `docker build` against this ignore file).
web/test
web/tests
web/playwright.config.ts
web/vitest.config.ts
web/scripts
# Throwaway output directories from `test/export/unconfigured-build-fails.test.ts`.
web/.build-guard-out-*

# ---- Artifact staging ------------------------------------------------------
# `web/data-derived/` is DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED: it is the documented path
# for staging a real exported artifact into the build context for
# `--build-arg EXPORT_DIR=data-derived` (see Dockerfile's web-builder stage).
#
# The root-level `.e2e-export-artifact/` that
# `.github/workflows/ingest-export-build.yml` writes IS excluded: no COPY line
# reads it, so in the build context it would be dead weight that looks usable.
.e2e-export-artifact
